{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>According to the number of years after the jubilee you shall buy.</b> This is its plain sense, to set the verse on its face: it comes to warn about fraud. When you sell or buy land, know how many years there are until the jubilee; according to the years and the produce the field is fit to yield, the seller shall sell and the buyer shall buy — for in the end it returns to him in the jubilee year. If there are few years and the seller sells it for a high price, the buyer has been defrauded; and if there are many years and the buyer has eaten much produce from it, the seller has been defrauded. Therefore one must buy it according to the time. And this is what is said: ״בְּמִסְפַּר שְׁנֵי תְבוּאֹת יִמְכַּר לָךְ״ — according to the count of the years of produce that it will stand in the hand of the buyer, you shall sell it to him. And our Sages derived from here that one who sells his field may not redeem it in less than two years — that it stand two years in the hand of the buyer from day to day, even if there are three harvests in those two years, such as when he sold it to him already sown; and 'two' does not depart from its plain sense — that is, a count of years of produce and not of blight, and the minimum of years is two (Sifra; Arakhin 29)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:18.895958571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}